{
  "technical_and_design_decisions": [
    "The implementation will be done in Go, extending the existing Hyperledger Fabric `fabric-config` library.",
    "The CLI tool will be developed as a separate binary within the repository, likely using the `cobra` library for CLI parsing, consistent with other Fabric tools.",
    "New API functions will follow the existing fluent interface pattern of the library (e.g., `c.Orderer().Organization(\"org\")`).",
    "The CLI tool will use standard Go JSON unmarshalling for input files (batch operations, connection profile, signing identities).",
    "For U3, the `OrdererAddresses` field will be made read-only in the API, and a new `RemoveLegacyOrdererAddresses` function will be added to the top-level channel group.",
    "For U7 and U8, individual setter functions will internally fetch the current configuration, modify the specific field, and persist the changes, preserving other existing values."
  ],
  "assumptions": [
    "The developer is highly experienced with Go and Hyperledger Fabric internals.",
    "Existing CI/CD pipelines and test infrastructure are available and do not require setup.",
    "The 'examples' mentioned in the specification refer to Go code examples within the repository, not a separate documentation website.",
    "1 workday equals 8 hours of focused development effort.",
    "The CLI tool will support the specific operations listed in U6 and will return an error for unsupported operations as required."
  ],
  "activities": [
    {
      "activity_id": "A1",
      "activity_name": "Consortium Management",
      "activity_description": "Implement function to add a new consortium to the consortiums group, handle edge cases for empty orgs, and update examples (U1).",
      "most_likely_effort": 1.5
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A2",
      "activity_name": "Unsigned Config Update",
      "activity_description": "Implement function to return a cb.ConfigUpdateEnvelope without requiring signing identities (U2).",
      "most_likely_effort": 1.0
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A3",
      "activity_name": "Legacy Orderer Addresses Removal",
      "activity_description": "Implement RemoveLegacyOrdererAddresses function, prevent updates to OrdererAddresses, and update genesis block creation logic (U3).",
      "most_likely_effort": 2.0
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A4",
      "activity_name": "Kafka Brokers Removal",
      "activity_description": "Implement function to remove KafkaBrokers section for Kafka to EtcdRaft migration and update examples (U4).",
      "most_likely_effort": 1.5
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A5",
      "activity_name": "Consenter Management",
      "activity_description": "Implement AddConsenter and RemoveConsenter functions for EtcdRaft orderer configuration, ensuring removal matches all 4 fields (U5).",
      "most_likely_effort": 2.5
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A6",
      "activity_name": "Orderer Individual Field Updates",
      "activity_description": "Implement individual setter functions for OrdererGroup (SetMaxMessageCount, SetBatchTimeout, SetConsensusType, etc.) and update examples (U7).",
      "most_likely_effort": 4.0
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A7",
      "activity_name": "MSP Individual Field Updates",
      "activity_description": "Implement individual setter functions for MSP config across Org groups (Add/Remove Root, Admin, TLS certs, CRLs, OUIdentifiers, etc.) and update examples (U8).",
      "most_likely_effort": 5.0
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A8",
      "activity_name": "CLI Tool Core",
      "activity_description": "Develop CLI structure, JSON parsing for batch operations, connection profile, and signing identities (U6).",
      "most_likely_effort": 4.0
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A9",
      "activity_name": "CLI Tool Operations",
      "activity_description": "Implement supported bulk operations (Update MSP, Remove/Add consenter, Update TLS certs, Remove/Add anchor peers) (U6).",
      "most_likely_effort": 5.0
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A10",
      "activity_name": "CLI Tool Execution & Dry-run",
      "activity_description": "Implement config block fetching via discovery, dry-run mode, and transaction submission (U6).",
      "most_likely_effort": 4.0
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A11",
      "activity_name": "Testing & Documentation",
      "activity_description": "Write unit tests for all new library functions and integration tests for the CLI tool. Update README and documentation.",
      "most_likely_effort": 5.0
    }
  ],
  "reported_total": {
    "most_likely_effort": 35.5
  }
}
```

